  "body": "**What:** `solid_law_goldens::every_posted_golden_is_a_program_the_gate_passes` (#862, #1000) judges every posted `.nc` golden whose stem has a `.cl` golden. Since #1000 its `UNJUDGED` list holds one entry: `arc_planes`. That program is hand-built in `crates/app/tests/arc_planes.rs` (a G18 and a G19 arc between XY arcs, for the five dialect posts). No operation kind, part, region or tool record makes it, so no gate a user's post runs can judge it. The guard can't tell a synthetic posting fixture from an op program nobody judged, so it keeps a by-name exception list.\n\n**Why it matters:** a by-name exception list is where an unjudged op golden can hide later. A synthetic fixture should say what it is in the golden itself, the way a refused program carries the \"refused program, posted for syntax conformance\" first line.\n\n**Done means:** posted goldens of hand-built posting fixtures (today `arc_planes` in Fanuc, haas, mazak, sinumerik, heidenhain) carry a first-line marker the guard recognises (e.g. \"synthetic program, posted for syntax conformance\"), written by the suite's regeneration path (`WRITE_GOLDEN=1 cargo test -p camcraft-app --test arc_planes`) and not by hand. Alternatively the fixture gets a part and a gate that judges it. `UNJUDGED` is then empty and removed, so any new unjudged posted golden fails the guard.\n\nFound by the #1000 worker. Part of #1000's follow-up.\n",
